I changed the last line of `certificateLine` so a started certificate, interim or not, ends with `, N days left` (or `, 1 day left`), or `, lapsed` when no days remain. The no-certificate and not-yet-started lines are untouched.

I couldn't see whether `expires` is the last day the boat may go out or the first day it may not. I assumed it is the first day it may not, so the days left are `expires - today` and the line says lapsed once `today >= expires`. If `expires` is actually the last valid day, change `left` to `cert.expires - today + 1`. The check in `currentCertificate` or `isCertified` (around lines 319–330) would show which is right.
